  "textContent": "A rehearsal for the television special James Paul McCartney took place on 17 March 1973 at Elstree Studios. The rehearsal came the day before Wings performed in the studios before an audience of fans.Produced by ATV, James Paul McCartney was first broadcast on 16 April 1973 in the USA, and 10 May in the UK. It was released on DVD as part of the super deluxe reissue of in Red Rose Speedway December 2018.\n\n\n\n\n\nPage last updated: 28 November 2025Also on this day...2013: Blue plaque for Lennon and Harrison unveiled at the Apple Boutique building2009: Struggling Penny Lane businesses ask for help2009: Ringo to release book of Beatles photographs?2003: Album release: Back In The World by Paul McCartney1993: Paul McCartney live: Sydney Entertainment Centre, Sydney1978: US single release: With A Little Luck by Wings1977: Recording: B Side To Seaside by Suzy And The Red Stripes1975: Recording: Spirits Of Ancient Egypt by Wings1975: Joe English joins Wings1972: Recording: Loup (1st Indian On The Moon) by Wings1969: John Lennon and Yoko Ono fly to Paris1968: Pattie Harrison celebrates her 24th birthday in India1967: Recording: She’s Leaving Home1965: Filming: Help!, Austria1964: Filming: A Hard Day’s Night1963: The Beatles live: Embassy Cinema, Peterborough1962: The Beatles live: Knotty Ash Village Hall, Liverpool1961: The Beatles live: Liverpool Jazz Society, Liverpool1961: The Beatles live: Mossway Hall, Liverpool1944: Pattie Boyd is bornWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
